Overlay patch 0034: stereoscopic eye rendering for visionOS 3D
(= sibling ports' 0044/reference 0031, rebased onto Starship's OLDER LUS layout
src/graphic/Fast3D/; VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK §2.4/§2.5).

In 3D (gSoh3DMode, shell-owned) Fast3dWindow runs the interpreter TWICE per host
frame (same game time) with an eye state that swaps mGameFb to a per-eye
framebuffer and applies an off-axis stereo projection to PERSPECTIVE matrices
only, folded in the SF64 camera basis exported by 0035. fb 0 (the hidden
window's drawable) is never touched in 3D; EndFrameOffscreen commits the drawn
framebuffers, rides 0024's pending-mip pass, and publishes eye textures ON GPU
COMPLETION (double-buffered per eye — the compositor blit-copies with no
cross-queue fence, the §2.4 device-only trap).

Port deltas vs the sibling patch:
- Starship LUS is the OLD layout: src/graphic/Fast3D/{interpreter,Fast3dWindow}
  + src/graphic/Fast3D/backends/{gfx_metal,gfx_rendering_api}. Member names
  (mDrawnFramebuffers, mHasEndedEncoding, mFrameAutoreleasePool,
  sSohIosPendingMips, FramebufferMetal.*) match verbatim.
- Context::GetRawInstance() -> GetInstance() (our fork has only that accessor).
- SSAA gate: Starship's 0026 SSAA block (StartFrame, default 2.0) must NOT run
  during an eye pass or the eye fb resizes twice/frame — gate on sSoh3DEye == 0.
- v1 MENU STUB: the two-pass loop does NOT composite the menu into the eyes
  (that needs the Gui split, a follow-up). 3D renders stereo; the menu stays
  reachable in 2D. gpu-ms 0027 completion handler kept honest in 3D.

Shell globals live in SohIosShell.m (linked on iPhone too, mode stays 0);
__IOS__-guarded so the macOS build (which compiles this overlaid vendor) uses
the base-class no-op virtuals. Camera basis + comfort flags come from 0035.


